# Coder Agent

A **ReAct** agent runs a tight **think → act → observe** loop, and its actions are
sandboxed `bash` tools. Same `agent` primitive as the [[The Analyst Agent]] — only
the tools differ. The loop runs in server Elixir; the *tools* run in a sandbox, so
the agent can edit and run real code without touching anything ungranted.

@coder grant: [:fs, :exec], memory: "256mb", timeout: 60_000

server sandbox :repl, @coder do
  defmodule Tools do
    def read_file(path), do: File.read(path)
    def edit_file(path, find, replace), do: File.write(path, String.replace(File.read!(path), find, replace))
    # Sandbox.exec goes through the Dock — the :exec grant is what makes it work.
    def run_tests(focus), do: Sandbox.exec("work", ["test", focus])
  end
end

agent :coder do
  model "minimax/minimax-m3"
  tools [Tools.read_file/1, Tools.edit_file/3, Tools.run_tests/1]

  system """
  Fix a failing test in strict ReAct turns: one thought, one tool call.
  Run the test, read the unit, make the smallest edit, re-run. Never edit a test
  to make it pass.
  """
end

The trace is typed memory — there's no hidden state on the model:

defmodule Step do
  defstruct thought: "", action: nil, observation: nil
end

A run against a broken [[Score]]: run the test → see `expected 70, got 35` → read the
unit → halve a doubled divisor → re-run → green. There's no turn cap, only `timeout:`.
Next: [[Researcher]].
